{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","book":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible","chapter":638,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:jfb:Prov.10","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","authorshipDateRange":"19th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Protestant","translator":null,"edition":"1871 one-volume text; expanded electronic edition by Ernie Stefanik","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"jfb","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"searchIndexed":false},"originalBook":"Proverbs","sourceVolumeId":"jfb","source":{"id":"jfb","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"title":"Proverbs 10","reference":"Proverbs 10","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Pr 10:1-32.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":2,"text":"Here begins the second part of the book, Pr 10:1-22:16, which, with the third, Pr 22:16-25:28, contains series of proverbs whose sense is complete in one or two verses, and which, having no logical connection, admit of no analysis.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":3,"text":"The parallelisms of Pr 10:1-15:33 are mostly antithetic; and those of Pr 16:1-22:16, synthetic.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":4,"text":"The evidences of art in the structure are very clear, and indicate, probably, a purpose of facilitating the labor of memorizing.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":5,"text":"1. wise [and] foolish—as they follow or reject the precepts of wisdom.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":6,"text":"maketh … father—or, \"gladdens a father.\"","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":7,"text":"heaviness—or, \"grief.\"","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":9,"text":"Treasures … nothing—that is, Ill-gotten gains give no true happiness (compare Pr 4:17; Mt 6:19).","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":10,"text":"righteousness—especially beneficence (Ps 112:9).","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":11,"text":"death—the greatest of all evils.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":12,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":13,"text":"(Compare Ps 37:16-20).","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":14,"text":"The last clause is better: \"He will repel the greedy desires of the wicked.\"","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":15,"text":"4. slack—literally, \"deceitful,\" failing of its purpose (compare Ho 7:16).","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":16,"text":"maketh rich—(compare Pr 10:22).","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":17,"text":"5. son—as Pr 1:8, 10, and often.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":18,"text":"sleepeth—in indolence, and not for rest.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":19,"text":"causeth shame—literally, \"is base\" (compare Pr 14:35; 17:2).","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":20,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":21,"text":"Blessings—literally, \"Praises.\"","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":22,"text":"The last clause is better: \"The mouth of the wicked covereth (or concealeth) violence (or mischievous devices)\" to be executed in due time (Ps 5:9; 10:7; Ro 3:14), and hence has no praises (compare Pr 10:11).","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":23,"text":"7. blessed—literally, \"for a blessing,\" or praise.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":24,"text":"shall rot—literally, \"be worm-eaten,\" useless and disgusting.","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":25,"text":"8. wise, &c.—(compare Pr 9:8, 9, 16), opposed to","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":26,"text":"prating fool—or, \"fool of lips of wicked language.\"","sourceParagraph":18,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":27,"text":"fall—headlong, suddenly.","sourceParagraph":19,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":28,"text":"9. perverteth his ways—acts deceitfully.","sourceParagraph":20,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":29,"text":"known—discovered and punished.","sourceParagraph":21,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":30,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":22,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":31,"text":"Two vices contrasted; hypocrisy, or insinuating evil against one (Pr 6:13; Ps 35:19), and rashness of speech.","sourceParagraph":22,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":32,"text":"In each case, the results are on the evildoers.","sourceParagraph":22,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":33,"text":"11. a well—or, \"source\" of good to himself and others (Joh 7:37, 38).","sourceParagraph":23,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":34,"text":"On last clause, see on Pr 10:6.","sourceParagraph":23,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":35,"text":"12. strifes—or, \"litigations.\"","sourceParagraph":24,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":36,"text":"covereth—by forgiveness and forbearance.","sourceParagraph":25,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":37,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":26,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":38,"text":"In the lips … found—hence, not beaten, as the wicked-speaking fool.","sourceParagraph":26,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":39,"text":"void of understanding—(Pr 6:32; 7:7).","sourceParagraph":27,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":40,"text":"14. lay up knowledge—that is, as treasures for good use.","sourceParagraph":28,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":41,"text":"mouth … destruction—or, \"as to the mouth,\" &c., destruction is near; they expose themselves to evil by prating.","sourceParagraph":29,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":42,"text":"15.","sourceParagraph":30,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":43,"text":"Both by trusting in \"uncertain riches\" (1Ti 6:17), or by the evils of poverty (Pr 30:9), men, not fearing God, fall into dangers.","sourceParagraph":30,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":44,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":31,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":45,"text":"The industry of the righteous is alone truly successful, while the earnings of the wicked tempt and lead to sin.","sourceParagraph":31,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":46,"text":"17. keepeth—observes (Pr 3:18; 4:22).","sourceParagraph":32,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":47,"text":"refuseth—or, \"turns from reproof,\" which might direct him aright.","sourceParagraph":33,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":48,"text":"18.","sourceParagraph":34,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":49,"text":"Both vices must one day be known and punished, and hence their folly.","sourceParagraph":34,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":50,"text":"19.","sourceParagraph":35,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":51,"text":"Much speech involves risk of sin; hence the wisdom of restraining the tongue (Ps 39:1; Jas 1:26).","sourceParagraph":35,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":52,"text":"20.","sourceParagraph":36,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":53,"text":"Right speech is the fruit of a good heart, but the wicked show theirs to be useless.","sourceParagraph":36,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":54,"text":"21.","sourceParagraph":37,"scriptureVerseStart":21,"scriptureVerseEnd":21},{"verse":55,"text":"Fools not only fail to benefit others, as do the righteous, but procure their own ruin (compare Pr 10:11, 17; Ho 4:6).","sourceParagraph":37,"scriptureVerseStart":21,"scriptureVerseEnd":21},{"verse":56,"text":"22. it maketh, &c.—\"it\" is emphatic.","sourceParagraph":38,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":57,"text":"Riches from God are without the sorrow of ill-gotten wealth (compare Ec 2:21-23; 1Ti 6:9, 10, 17).","sourceParagraph":38,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":58,"text":"23.","sourceParagraph":39,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":59,"text":"Sin is the pleasure of the wicked; wisdom that of the good.","sourceParagraph":39,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":60,"text":"24. it—the very thing.","sourceParagraph":40,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":61,"text":"The wicked get dreaded evil; the righteous, desired good.","sourceParagraph":40,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":62,"text":"25.","sourceParagraph":41,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":63,"text":"(Compare Ps 1:4; 37:9, 10, 36).","sourceParagraph":41,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":64,"text":"righteous … foundation—well laid and firm (Mt 7:24, 25).","sourceParagraph":42,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":65,"text":"26. that is, causes vexation.","sourceParagraph":43,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":66,"text":"27.","sourceParagraph":44,"scriptureVerseStart":27,"scriptureVerseEnd":27},{"verse":67,"text":"(Compare Pr 9:11; Ps 55:23).","sourceParagraph":44,"scriptureVerseStart":27,"scriptureVerseEnd":27},{"verse":68,"text":"28. gladness—in confidence of realizing it.","sourceParagraph":45,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":69,"text":"expectation … perish—in disappointment.","sourceParagraph":46,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":70,"text":"29.","sourceParagraph":47,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":71,"text":"The way, &c.—that is, God's providence sustains the righteous and overthrows the wicked (Ho 14:9).","sourceParagraph":47,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":72,"text":"30.","sourceParagraph":48,"scriptureVerseStart":30,"scriptureVerseEnd":30},{"verse":73,"text":"(Compare Pr 12:3; Ps 37:9-11; 102:28).","sourceParagraph":48,"scriptureVerseStart":30,"scriptureVerseEnd":30},{"verse":74,"text":"earth—or, \"land of promise.\"","sourceParagraph":49,"scriptureVerseStart":30,"scriptureVerseEnd":30},{"verse":75,"text":"31. bringeth forth—literally, \"germinates\" as a plant.","sourceParagraph":50,"scriptureVerseStart":31,"scriptureVerseEnd":31},{"verse":76,"text":"froward—(Compare Pr 2:12, 14).","sourceParagraph":51,"scriptureVerseStart":31,"scriptureVerseEnd":31},{"verse":77,"text":"cut off—as an unproductive plant.","sourceParagraph":52,"scriptureVerseStart":31,"scriptureVerseEnd":31},{"verse":78,"text":"32. know—regard and provide for (Ps 1:6).","sourceParagraph":53,"scriptureVerseStart":32,"scriptureVerseEnd":32},{"verse":79,"text":"frowardness—all kinds of deceit and ill-nature.","sourceParagraph":54,"scriptureVerseStart":32,"scriptureVerseEnd":32},{"verse":80,"text":"The word is plural.","sourceParagraph":54,"scriptureVerseStart":32,"scriptureVerseEnd":32}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":10}}